 ## shell.css
 
-### §container-not-viewport — the shell responds to its own width
+### §viewport-media-query — the shell's layout step uses a viewport media query
+- Since: 2026-10-23
+- Decision: the shell's layout step uses `@media (min-width: 720px)`.
+- Supersedes: §container-not-viewport (2026-09-15), which required `@container` queries on `.shell` and forbade
+  viewport `@media` width queries. The maintainer explicitly named that decision and overrode it on 2026-10-23.
+- Note: the earlier reason is not refuted by this change. The shell renders inside split panes as narrow as 380px on a
+  1440px screen, and a viewport query picks the two-column layout there, which clips the sidebar (incident 2026-09-14).
+  The maintainer accepted that trade-off.
+
+### §container-not-viewport — SUPERSEDED 2026-10-23 by §viewport-media-query
